{{-- Reviews are opinion, not findings of fact (bench-review#54).

    One line, one wording, three surfaces — the judge profile header, the
    reviews feed and the article page. It exists because of where a dispute
    starts: a judge's counsel reads the page the review is on, not the Terms,
    and "we said so on /terms" is a weaker position than the statement being
    visible next to the content it describes.

    Deliberately markup-only: no <script>, so there is no component scope to
    register and nothing that can fail to hydrate. A disclaimer that depends
    on JavaScript having booted is a disclaimer that is absent exactly when
    the page is being screenshotted. --}}
<p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-500 text-xs">
  Reviews on Bench Review are the opinions of individual users, not verified
  statements of fact, and are not endorsed by any court.
  <StxLink to="/terms" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-gray-700">Terms of Service</StxLink>
</p>
